<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Basil's Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1555–1561</span> · Also known as Cathedral of Vasily the Blessed</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Basil's Cathedral, formally the Cathedral of the Intercession of the Most Holy Theotokos on the Moat, stands on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-square">Red Square</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> had it built in 1555–1561 to commemorate the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazan">Kazan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astrakhan">Astrakhan</a>, and its cluster of chapels crowned with colourful onion domes made it a symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It takes its popular name from the holy fool Basil, buried in a chapel added in 1588.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-basils-cathedral.jpg" alt="Saint Basil's Cathedral" width="320" height="355" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tsy1980 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Basil%27s_Cathedral_in_Moscow.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
